# Start robot: the first button of the operator console (ADR-0071).
#
# Enables the robot. Where a physical side RUNS (ADR-0072: not on a pair started
# with the plant alone) the console first reads the twin's mode as SIM and asks
# the operator to clear the cell (ConfirmOperator, with ConsoleState.prompt),
# because the initializer may home the physical track and bring the carriage to
# the program's start (InitializeAsset.srv); only then does it initialize every
# running physical side's arm (`InitializeAsset`, on that side's own domain).
# Where no physical side runs nothing is asked and nothing is initialized. Then it reads the plant arm's custody and refuses an arm that
# says it holds a part. Commands no arm motion of its own. Until it succeeds the
# console refuses Home and Start program. Refused while another request runs.
#
# Served under the plan's `console.start_robot` (ConsoleState.msg).
---
bool success   # the arm is started; the console is READY
string detail  # what was done, or why it was refused or failed
